-- title:
--   Uniqueness of the Drinfeld-pinned refinement of an Igusa ring, q=2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q = 2$, a level $M'\ne 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set). Assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the former along $A$ onto $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$ (a valuation subring with a surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and with orders of divisors), agreeing coefficientwise with reduction of Laurent series over $A$. Further data: $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; an index $\zeta$ of primitive $q$-th roots of unity; families $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig},\ell}$ ($\ell \in \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$) and $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss},s}$ ($s \in W$) of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, subject to the Igusa hypotheses (description of $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig},\infty}$ by quotients of Laurent series over $A$ with non-vanishing reduced denominator, transitivity of the family under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ realising $\ell$, injectivity of $\ell \mapsto \mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig},\ell}$, and permutation of the family by all such automorphisms) and to the supersingular hypotheses ($\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss},s}$ meets the constants exactly in $A$, is invariant under the $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$ automorphisms, contains functions with $j$-pole-free $R_0$-reduction in the valuation ring at $s$ together with the prescribed residue, and carries an element all of whose translates by constants from $A$ are units); and the descent data consisting of a subfield $K_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi \in K_0$, a henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with an injective local homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image is $A \cap K_0$, with surjective composite to the residue field of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi_0$ satisfying $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$, the subfield $F_0 \subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, which contains the image $\hat\jmath$ of $j$, and an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ induced by $\iota$. Let $\ell$ be a point of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, $s \in W$, and let $V, V'$ be valuation subrings of $F_0$ such that both map into $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig},\ell}$, both omit some element of $F_0$ lying in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig},\ell}$, and both have the property that every $g \in F_0$ integral over $A_0[\hat\jmath]$ whose image lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss},s}$ is a non-unit of $V$ (respectively of $V'$). Then $V = V'$.
--
--   On the Igusa leg of the semistable covering of the full-level modular curve, this is the uniqueness statement saying that a proper refinement of the traced Igusa ring $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig},\ell} \cap F_0$ pinned down by a supersingular (Drinfeld) place $s$ is unique: the Igusa component $\ell$ has at most one such place over the floor place $s$. It is the $q = 2$ case, and it feeds the construction of Igusa and node charts for the normal model generated by $j$.
